(begin-tx "DPDC-G2 — argument-domain guards: pause state, description, royalty precision, holding")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
;;==== DPDC-G2 — argument-domain guards: pause state, description, royalty precision, holding · 01 · namespace ==== 
(print "--- [DPDC-G2 — argument-domain guards: pause state, description, royalty precision, holding · 01 · namespace] ---")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [DPDC-G2 · 01 · four guards that need no fixture state] ---")
;;P3.3. Four guards whose rejecting input is an ARGUMENT rather than a state, so they need no
;;fixture beyond a collection that already exists. Sorted by shape rather than by module: this is
;;the cheapest class and it is worth exhausting before building anything.
;;==== DPDC-G2 — argument-domain guards: pause state, description, royalty precision, holding · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [DPDC-G2 — argument-domain guards: pause state, description, royalty precision, holding · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (ref-DPDC:module{DpdcV2} DPDC)
        (nf:string "MOCKN-98c486052a51")
    )
    (map print
        [
            ;;--- 1] UEV_PauseState takes the EXPECTED answer as an argument, so the state=true
            ;;    branch (require paused) is reachable on an UNPAUSED collection with no setup.
            ;;    Its state=false branch needs a PAUSED one, which no client path produces -- see
            ;;    DPDC-G2b just below, where `env-module-admin` supplies the state directly and both
            ;;    arms are then driven in both states.
            (expect "<<DPDC-G2>> MOCKN is not paused" false (ref-DPDC::UR_IsPaused nf false))
            (expect "<<DPDC-G2>> UEV_PauseState accepts <state> false, which is the live value"
                true (!= "" (format "{}" [(ref-DPDC::UEV_PauseState nf false false)])))
            (expect-failure "<<DPDC-G2>> UEV_PauseState rejects <state> true while UNPAUSED"
                "is already unpaused" (ref-DPDC::UEV_PauseState nf false true))
            ;;--- 2] UEV_Description bounds a nonce's free text at 1024 words (audit #12Hb).
            ;;    Built rather than typed: 1025 single-character words is one past the bound, and
            ;;    the happy path one below it proves the bound is where the message says it is.
            ;;    OFF-BY-ONE, worth stating: "w " repeated N times ends in a SPACE, so splitting on
            ;;    " " yields N+1 words (the last empty). N=1023 is therefore exactly 1024 words --
            ;;    the bound -- and N=1024 is 1025, one past it. The first draft used 1024/1025 and
            ;;    the ACCEPTED case failed, which is how the extra word surfaced.
            (expect "<<DPDC-G2>> a description of exactly 1024 words is accepted"
                true (!= "" (format "{}" [(ref-DPDC::UEV_Description (concat (make-list 1023 "w ")))])))
            (expect-failure "<<DPDC-G2>> ...and one word more is refused"
                "Nonce description cannot exceed 1024 words"
                (ref-DPDC::UEV_Description (concat (make-list 1024 "w "))))
            ;;--- 3] UEV_IgnisRoyalty: pure precision check against the IGNIS token's decimals.
            (expect-failure "<<DPDC-G2>> UEV_IgnisRoyalty rejects a royalty finer than IGNIS precision"
                "is not conform with its precision"
                (ref-DPDC::UEV_IgnisRoyalty 0.00000000000000000000000001))
            ;;--- 4] UEV_NonceQuantityInclusion, NFT branch (son=false, positive nonce): the nonce
            ;;    HOLDER is compared against the account, so this is a 2x2 on ownership rather
            ;;    than a one-sided rejection. DPDC-03 above transfers MOCKN nonce 1 to EMMA, so
            ;;    EMMA is the holder here and ANHD is not -- both cells come free from that.
            ;;    (The first draft assumed EMMA was a NON-holder and the rejection passed as a
            ;;    success, which is the giveaway that the fixture had already moved the nonce.)
            (expect "<<DPDC-G2>> the guard ACCEPTS the account that holds NFT nonce 1"
                true (!= "" (format "{}" [(ref-DPDC::UEV_NonceQuantityInclusion KST.EMMA nf false 1 1)])))
            (expect-failure "<<DPDC-G2>> ...and REJECTS one that does not"
                "doesnt hold NFT" (ref-DPDC::UEV_NonceQuantityInclusion KST.ANHD nf false 1 1))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;|| DPDC-G2b — the pause arm DPDC-G2 could not reach, reached.
;;
(begin-tx "DPDC-G2b - the state=false arm of UEV_PauseState, on a genuinely paused collection")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
;;==== DPDC-G2b - the state=false arm of UEV_PauseState, on a genuinely paused collection · 01 · namespace ==== 
(print "--- [DPDC-G2b - the state=false arm of UEV_PauseState, on a genuinely paused collection · 01 · namespace] ---")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [DPDC-G2b · 01 · UEV_PauseState, the other arm] ---")
;;DPDC-G2 above recorded that the `state=false` arm "needs a paused one and is not reachable here",
;;and left it on the worklist. It IS reachable: `is-paused` is an ordinary field of
;;`DPNF|T|Properties`, and `env-module-admin` grants this module's admin inside a REPL, so the
;;collection can be driven into the paused state directly and the whole thing discarded by
;;`rollback-tx`. That is the same technique that opened LIQUID's three "unreachable" guards.
;;
;;Writing the field rather than calling a pause CLIENT is deliberate and is the honest thing to do
;;here: DPDC-G3 establishes that a collection's property flags are fixed at issuance, so there is no
;;client path that pauses MOCKN at all. The field write reproduces the STATE a paused collection is
;;in without pretending a route to it exists. What is being pinned is the guard's reading of that
;;state, which is exactly what the guard is for.
;;==== DPDC-G2b - the state=false arm of UEV_PauseState, on a genuinely paused collection · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [DPDC-G2b - the state=false arm of UEV_PauseState, on a genuinely paused collection · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (ref-DPDC:module{DpdcV2} DPDC)
        (nf:string "MOCKN-98c486052a51")
    )
    (env-module-admin DPDC)
    (update DPDC.DPNF|T|Properties nf { "is-paused" : true })
    (map print
        [
            (expect "<<DPDC-G2b>> MOCKN now reads as paused" true (ref-DPDC::UR_IsPaused nf false))
            ;;THE ITEM: the arm DPDC-G2 could only describe. Asking for "not paused" on a paused
            ;;collection names the state that tripped it, which is the wording DPTF-G1 fixed in the
            ;;sibling module and DPDC already had right.
            (expect-failure "<<DPDC-G2b>> UEV_PauseState rejects <state> false while PAUSED"
                "is already paused" (ref-DPDC::UEV_PauseState nf false false))
            ;;and the arm that was reachable before flips WITH the state -- which is what proves the
            ;;guard reads `is-paused` and is not simply constant in one direction. Both arms of this
            ;;guard have now been driven in both states: a full 2x2, not two half-truths.
            (expect "<<DPDC-G2b>> ...while <state> true, refused in DPDC-G2, is now accepted"
                true (!= "" (format "{}" [(ref-DPDC::UEV_PauseState nf false true)])))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
;;the pause is discarded -- DPDC-G2c checks it
(rollback-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;|| DPDC-G2c — the pause flip left no trace.
;;
(begin-tx "DPDC-G2c - no leakage")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [DPDC-G2c · 01 · no leakage] ---")
;;MOCKN is used by later transactions in this file and by the DPDC scenario suites. A leaked pause
;;would not fail loudly here -- it would surface much later as a transfer refusal in an unrelated
;;test, so it is asserted at the seam instead.
(print
    (expect "<<DPDC-G2c>> MOCKN is unpaused again"
        false (DPDC.UR_IsPaused "MOCKN-98c486052a51" false)))
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;|| DPDC-G2d — the OR-shaped ownership gate, driven from all three sides.
;;
(begin-tx "DPDC-G2d - CAP_OwnerOrCreator: owner OK, creator OK, third party refused")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [DPDC-G2d · 01 · enforce-one over two ownership predicates] ---")
;;`02_DPDC.pact:1288`. Unusual shape: an `enforce-one` over two `create-user-guard` wrappers, so it
;;passes when EITHER the owner or the creator signs. Its own message IS matchable (unlike the 40
;;inner messages nested inside enforce-one branch lists elsewhere in this campaign, which Pact never
;;surfaces) -- an enforce-one raises its OWN message when every branch fails, which is exactly the
;;case here.
;;
;;ALL THREE CELLS ARE DRIVEN, and for this shape that is the minimum that means anything. A single
;;refusal cannot distinguish "the OR works" from "the OR is broken and refuses everyone"; a single
;;acceptance cannot distinguish "either branch passes" from "only the first one is consulted". The
;;signature is switched between calls rather than the subject, so the token is held constant.
;;==== DPDC-G2d - CAP_OwnerOrCreator: owner OK, creator OK, third party refused · 01 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [DPDC-G2d - CAP_OwnerOrCreator: owner OK, creator OK, third party refused · 01 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (ref-DPDC:module{DpdcV2} DPDC)
        (nf:string "MOCKN-98c486052a51")
    )
    ;;the premise: for this fixture owner and creator are the SAME account, which is why the third
    ;;cell below has to be a genuinely unrelated signer rather than "the other one of the pair".
    (print
        (expect "<<DPDC-G2d>> MOCKN's owner and creator are both the patron"
            [KST.ANHD KST.ANHD]
            [(ref-DPDC::UR_OwnerKonto nf false) (ref-DPDC::UR_CreatorKonto nf false)]))
    (env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
    (print
        (expect "<<DPDC-G2d>> the owner/creator signature is accepted"
            true (!= "" (format "{}" [(ref-DPDC::CAP_OwnerOrCreator nf false)]))))
    ;;THE ITEM -- a real, funded account that is neither owner nor creator of this collection
    (env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
    (print
        (expect-failure "<<DPDC-G2d>> a third party satisfies NEITHER branch, so the enforce-one message fires"
            "Owner or Creator for DPNF MOCKN-98c486052a51 not verified"
            (ref-DPDC::CAP_OwnerOrCreator nf false)))
    ;;...and with NO signature at all, same message -- so the refusal is about the guard and not
    ;;about EMMA specifically.
    (env-sigs [])
    (print
        (expect-failure "<<DPDC-G2d>> ...and so does an unsigned call"
            "Owner or Creator for DPNF MOCKN-98c486052a51 not verified"
            (ref-DPDC::CAP_OwnerOrCreator nf false)))
    ;;the son=true arm names DPSF in the same message, so the discriminator is live text and not a
    ;;constant -- driven on a SemiFungible the suite already owns.
    (env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
    (print
        (expect-failure "<<DPDC-G2d>> ...and the son=true arm names DPSF, not DPNF"
            "Owner or Creator for DPSF MOCKS-98c486052a51 not verified"
            (ref-DPDC::CAP_OwnerOrCreator "MOCKS-98c486052a51" true)))
    ;;UEV_id, both arms. Pinned EXPLICITLY 2026-09-12 after they were found to have been credited
    ;;only by SHARED WORDING: a test in [4.0]_Sovereign-Executor.repl expected
    ;;"DPTF ID | does not exist", and `_enforce_coverage.py` matches by substring, so "ID {} does not
    ;;exist" was crediting these two DPDC sites as a side effect. When that expectation was rewritten
    ;;(the OUROBOROS mute-guard fix made its guard speak properly) the incidental credit vanished and
    ;;both showed up unpinned. **That is the tool's documented upper-bound caveat biting for real:
    ;;a guard credited through another module's wording is not actually proven.**
    (env-sigs [])
    (map print
        [
            (expect-failure "<<DPDC-G2d>> UEV_id names DPSF for an unknown semi-fungible"
                "DPSF ID NOSUCH-98c486052a51 does not exist"
                (ref-DPDC::UEV_id "NOSUCH-98c486052a51" true))
            (expect-failure "<<DPDC-G2d>> ...and DPNF for an unknown non-fungible"
                "DPNF ID NOSUCH-98c486052a51 does not exist"
                (ref-DPDC::UEV_id "NOSUCH-98c486052a51" false))
            ;;...and it ACCEPTS the collections this suite really built, so the two refusals are
            ;;about the id being unknown and not about the guard rejecting everything.
            (expect "<<DPDC-G2d>> ...while both real fixtures are accepted"
                true (!= "" (format "{}{}"
                    [(ref-DPDC::UEV_id "MOCKS-98c486052a51" true)
                     (ref-DPDC::UEV_id "MOCKN-98c486052a51" false)])))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
