(begin-tx "DPDC-G15 — the citizen minter's position-count parity check")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 150000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== DPDC-G15 — the citizen minter's position-count parity check · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== ====
(print "--- [DPDC-G15 — the citizen minter's position-count parity check · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(print "--- [DPDC-G15 · 01 · metadata rows must match the positions being spawned] ---")
;;`KBN::C_Spawn` (2_CITIZEN/4_BunniesMinter) batches an NFT mint: it takes a count of positions and one
;;metadata row per position, and refuses when the two disagree -- otherwise collectables would be minted
;;with metadata the caller never supplied for them.
;;
;;WHY IT LIVES IN THIS FILE. KBN is a CITIZEN minter and has no harness of its own, but it is deployed by
;;`deploy-stage02.repl`, which this file already loads -- and it mints DPNF collectables, so the subject
;;matter belongs with DPDC anyway. The alternative homes (the Kursan AQP suites) cost 2-7x the wall time
;;for the same assertion. Worth remembering when a citizen module's only guard is argument-domain: find
;;the cheapest harness that DEPLOYS it rather than the one that conceptually owns it.
(map print
    [
        (expect-failure "<<DPDC-G15>> two metadata rows against three positions is refused"
            "Invalid Number of Positions"
            (KBN.C_Spawn KST.ANHD "KBN-98c486052a51" 1 3 [["a"] ["b"]]))
        ;;...and the other direction, so the check is parity rather than a floor on either side
        (expect-failure "<<DPDC-G15>> ...and so is three rows against two positions"
            "Invalid Number of Positions"
            (KBN.C_Spawn KST.ANHD "KBN-98c486052a51" 1 2 [["a"] ["b"] ["c"]]))
    ]
)
(env-sigs [])
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
;;NOT PINNABLE, WITH THE PROOF — DPDC-C|C>REGISTER-NONCES' two amount branches.
;;
;;`03_DPDC-C.pact:279` "When Defining an SFT Set, {} must be equal to 0"
;;`03_DPDC-C.pact:282` "For an NFT Collectable the {} must be equal to 1"
;;
;;Both sit inside one nested `if` on (son, sft-set-mode):
;;    (if son
;;        (if sft-set-mode
;;            (enforce (= amount 0)  "When Defining an SFT Set, …")        <- :279
;;            (enforce (>= amount 0) "For an SFT Collectable, …"))          <- pinned by DPDC-G8
;;        (enforce (= amount 1) "For an NFT Collectable, …"))               <- :282
;;
;;EVERY CALLER IS KNOWN, and none of them can reach either. `C_CreateNewNonce` has exactly four call
;;sites in the codebase:
;;
;;    TS01 equivalent none — this is a Stage-02 client only
;;    TS02-C1.pact:450   (DPSF path)  id TRUE  0 (at 0 amount) … FALSE   -> the `(>= amount 0)` branch
;;    TS02-C2.pact:397   (DPNF path)  id FALSE 0 1              … FALSE   -> amount is the LITERAL 1
;;    08_DPDC-S.pact:1345 (NFT set)   id son   set-class 1      … TRUE    -> inside C_MakeNonFungibleSet,
;;                                                                           so `son` is FALSE there
;;    11_EQUITY+.pact:732               uses C_CreateNewNonce**s** (the multi form), whose capability
;;                                      hardcodes sft-set-mode FALSE
;;
;;So:
;;  * :282 needs son=FALSE with amount != 1 — and both son=FALSE callers pass the literal 1.
;;  * :279 needs son=TRUE **and** sft-set-mode=TRUE — a combination NO caller passes. The only
;;    sft-set-mode=TRUE site is the NFT set path, where son is false.
;;
;;AND THE SFT SET PATH DOES NOT GO THROUGH HERE AT ALL, which is the fact that settles :279.
;;`C_MakeSemiFungibleSet` (08_DPDC-S.pact:1253) credits an ALREADY-EXISTING set nonce via
;;`XB_CreditSFT-Nonce` rather than creating one — so the "defining an SFT set" case this guard names is
;;handled by a different function entirely. The guard is coherent, just unreachable.
;;
;;This is the same conclusion DPDC-G8 records for the DPNF path, generalised: **a guard's reachability
;;is a property of its call sites, not of the guard.** Worth stating as a proof rather than leaving two
;;items on the worklist reading as "needs a fixture" — there is no fixture that would help.
;;
;;PROPOSED, not applied: annotate both `;;UNREACHABLE`, which removes them from the worklist denominator
;;the way 19 other proven-unreachable sites already are.


;;|| NEXT >
;;|| DPDC-G16 — the cleanse that makes IGNIS|C>ROYALTY's amount guard unreachable.
;;
(begin-tx "DPDC-G16 - UC_CleanseAggregatedRoyalties drops zero-royalty creators")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
;;==== DPDC-G16 - UC_CleanseAggregatedRoyalties drops zero-royalty creators · 01 · namespace ==== =
(print "--- [DPDC-G16 - UC_CleanseAggregatedRoyalties drops zero-royalty creators · 01 · namespace] ---")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [DPDC-G16 · 01 · why 'Cannot debit|credit 0.0 or negative IGNIS amounts' cannot fire] ---")
;;`07_DPDC-T.pact:347` is annotated `;;UNREACHABLE via its only caller`. This block is what stops
;;that annotation from quietly becoming false.
;;
;;`ta` is not a client argument -- `C_IgnisRoyaltyCollector` is the only acquirer of IGNIS|C>ROYALTY
;;and reaches it through two filters:
;;  1. a zero TOTAL short-circuits to the NO-ROYALTY branch and never acquires this cap at all;
;;  2. `UC_CleanseAggregatedRoyalties` drops every creator whose royalty is 0.0, so the per-creator
;;     amounts handed to the cap are non-zero by construction.
;;Royalties are summed from unsigned per-nonce prices, so non-zero means positive.
;;
;;PURE COMPUTE, NO FIXTURE. The cleanse is a `UC_` over a constructed object, so this costs nothing
;;and does not depend on any collection existing -- which is what makes it worth asserting rather
;;than leaving as a comment. If the filter is ever weakened to, say, `>=`, these go red and the
;;guard becomes live and unpinned.
;;==== DPDC-G16 - UC_CleanseAggregatedRoyalties drops zero-royalty creators · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [DPDC-G16 - UC_CleanseAggregatedRoyalties drops zero-royalty creators · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (ref-DPDC-T:module{DpdcTransferV2} DPDC-T)
    )
    (let
        (
            (mixed:object{DpdcTransferV2.AggregatedRoyalties}
                (ref-DPDC-T::UDCx_AggregatedRoyalties ["a" "b" "c"] [1.5 0.0 2.5]))
        )
        (let
            (
                (cleansed:object{DpdcTransferV2.AggregatedRoyalties}
                    (ref-DPDC-T::UC_CleanseAggregatedRoyalties mixed))
            )
            (map print
                [
                    ;;the premise: the input really does contain a zero, so a pass below is not vacuous
                    (expect "<<DPDC-G16>> the input carries a zero-royalty creator"
                        true (contains 0.0 (at "ignis-royalties" mixed)))
                    ;;THE PROPERTY the annotation rests on
                    (expect "<<DPDC-G16>> the cleanse removes it, creators and royalties together"
                        [["a" "c"] [1.5 2.5]]
                        [(at "creators" cleansed) (at "ignis-royalties" cleansed)])
                    (expect "<<DPDC-G16>> ...so no amount the cap can be handed is 0.0"
                        false (contains 0.0 (at "ignis-royalties" cleansed)))
                    ;;and an all-non-zero input is returned untouched -- so the cleanse is a FILTER,
                    ;;not a rewrite. Without this the assertion above is also consistent with it
                    ;;mangling every input.
                    (expect "<<DPDC-G16>> ...while an already-clean aggregate passes through unchanged"
                        [["a" "b"] [1.5 2.5]]
                        (let ((clean:object{DpdcTransferV2.AggregatedRoyalties}
                                  (ref-DPDC-T::UC_CleanseAggregatedRoyalties
                                      (ref-DPDC-T::UDCx_AggregatedRoyalties ["a" "b"] [1.5 2.5]))))
                            [(at "creators" clean) (at "ignis-royalties" clean)]))
                ]
            )
            ""
        )
    )
)
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;|| DPDC-G17 — DPDC-T's own IGNIS debit bound.
;;
(begin-tx "DPDC-G17 - IGNIS|C>DEBIT: you cannot debit more IGNIS than the account holds")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== DPDC-G17 - IGNIS|C>DEBIT: you cannot debit more IGNIS than the account holds · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [DPDC-G17 - IGNIS|C>DEBIT: you cannot debit more IGNIS than the account holds · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(print "--- [DPDC-G17 · 01 · the royalty debit's balance bound] ---")
;;`07_DPDC-T.pact:378`. DPDC-T carries its OWN IGNIS debit capability for creator royalties, separate
;;from the one in 02_IGNIS -- and the two messages differ ("Insufficient IGNIS for Debiting" here,
;;"Insufficient GAS for GAS-Debiting" there), so neither credits the other. The IGNIS-module twin is
;;pinned by CONF-07; this one was not pinned anywhere.
;;
;;WHY THE CAP DIRECTLY RATHER THAN A CLIENT: through the real path (DPSF|C_TransferNonce and
;;friends) the amount is DERIVED -- a sum of per-nonce royalties, cleansed of zeros, on a collection
;;whose creator is not the sender. Driving it over the patron's balance would mean inflating a nonce
;;royalty first, i.e. building state to reach a bound that is a pure comparison. The bound itself is
;;the FIRST statement in the cap, before existence, type and ownership checks, so acquiring the cap
;;directly reaches it with nothing else able to answer -- the same technique CONF-07 uses on the twin.
;;==== DPDC-G17 - IGNIS|C>DEBIT: you cannot debit more IGNIS than the account holds · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [DPDC-G17 - IGNIS|C>DEBIT: you cannot debit more IGNIS than the account holds · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
    )
    (map print
        [
            ;;the premise: the patron holds SOME IGNIS, so the bound is a real comparison and not a
            ;;degenerate "zero balance refuses everything"
            (expect "<<DPDC-G17>> the patron holds IGNIS, so the bound is a genuine comparison"
                true (> (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply KST.ANHD false) 0.0))
            (expect-failure "<<DPDC-G17>> debiting more IGNIS than the account holds is refused"
                "Insufficient IGNIS for Debiting"
                (test-capability (DPDC-T.IGNIS|C>DEBIT KST.ANHD 999999999.0)))
            ;;...and an amount WITHIN the balance clears this enforce. It is the first statement in
            ;;the cap, so whatever answers next is by definition a later guard -- which is what shows
            ;;the refusal above is the balance bound and not the cap refusing outright.
            (expect "<<DPDC-G17>> ...while an amount within the balance clears it"
                true (!= "" (format "{}"
                    [(test-capability (DPDC-T.IGNIS|C>DEBIT KST.ANHD 0.000001))])))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;|| DPDC-G18 — the zero-supply debit guard on the credit/debit helper.
;;
(begin-tx "DPDC-G18 - XIv_CreditOrDebitDPDC: debiting a nonce with zero supply")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
;;==== DPDC-G18 - XIv_CreditOrDebitDPDC: debiting a nonce with zero supply · 01 · namespace ==== ==
(print "--- [DPDC-G18 - XIv_CreditOrDebitDPDC: debiting a nonce with zero supply · 01 · namespace] ---")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [DPDC-G18 · 01 · a debit against a nonce that holds nothing] ---")
;;`03_DPDC-C.pact:1073`. The helper reads the account's stored supply for the nonce and, when it is
;;zero, allows only a CREDIT -- `(if (= current-supply 0) (enforce cod "Cannot Debit 0 Amounts!"))`.
;;
;;ALMOST SHADOWED, and the margin is what makes the input specific. Through a client,
;;`DPDC::UEV_NonceQuantityInclusion` runs first in the acquiring capability and enforces
;;`(<= amount nonce-supply)`. With supply 0 that kills any amount > 0, and with no row at all it
;;kills amount = 0 too. The single surviving input is **amount = 0 against an existing row whose
;;supply is exactly 0** -- which is why this is driven on the helper directly rather than through a
;;transfer: the helper is a public unprotected defun (only the WRITE below it is IMC-gated), so the
;;enforce is reachable with nothing in the way.
;;
;;NO POSITIVE CONTROL IS POSSIBLE HERE, and that is worth stating rather than hiding: success falls
;;through to `XE_W|Supply`, which is `P|UEV_IMC`-gated and rejects an external caller. So the
;;accepting side is asserted indirectly -- a CREDIT (cod=true) gets past this enforce and dies at the
;;write instead, with a different message.
;;==== DPDC-G18 - XIv_CreditOrDebitDPDC: debiting a nonce with zero supply · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [DPDC-G18 - XIv_CreditOrDebitDPDC: debiting a nonce with zero supply · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (ref-DPDC-C:module{DpdcCreateV2} DPDC-C)
        (sf:string "MOCKS-98c486052a51")
    )
    (map print
        [
            (expect-failure "<<DPDC-G18>> debiting a nonce with zero supply is refused"
                "Cannot Debit 0 Amounts!"
                (ref-DPDC-C::XIv_CreditOrDebitDPDC "ghost-acct" sf true 1 0 false))
            ;;the same call as a CREDIT clears this enforce and is stopped by the policy gate on the
            ;;write below it -- a DIFFERENT message, which is what shows the refusal above is the
            ;;`cod` rule and not the helper refusing every call it is handed.
            (expect-failure "<<DPDC-G18>> ...while the same call as a CREDIT clears it and dies at the write"
                "None of the guards passed"
                (ref-DPDC-C::XIv_CreditOrDebitDPDC "ghost-acct" sf true 1 0 true))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;|| DPDC-G19 — the list-arity check on the mapped credit/debit helper.
;;
(begin-tx "DPDC-G19 - XIv_MappedCreditOrDebitDPDC: nonces and amounts must be the same length")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
;;==== DPDC-G19 - XIv_MappedCreditOrDebitDPDC: nonces and amounts must be the same length · 01 · namespace ==== 
(print "--- [DPDC-G19 - XIv_MappedCreditOrDebitDPDC: nonces and amounts must be the same length · 01 · namespace] ---")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [DPDC-G19 · 01 · mismatched nonce/amount list lengths] ---")
;;`03_DPDC-C.pact:1088`. The helper zips <nonces> against <amounts> by index, so unequal lengths
;;would either drop entries or index past the end of a list; the enforce makes the pairing total
;;before the map runs.
;;
;;IT IS A TAUTOLOGY THROUGH EVERY CLIENT PATH, which is why it needs driving directly. The client
;;entrypoints do not accept the two lists independently -- they build both from one source through
;;`U|INT::UC_NonceSplitter`, so the lengths agree by construction and no user input can separate
;;them. That makes this a data-integrity backstop for in-module callers rather than a client gate.
;;Unlike ANK's equivalent (see `modules/AQP.repl` <<AQP-G45>>, annotated UNREACHABLE) this one CAN
;;be executed: `XIv_MappedCreditOrDebitDPDC` is a public unprotected defun -- only the WRITE beneath
;;it is policy-gated -- so the enforce is reachable with nothing in front of it. The distinction is
;;the whole reason one is pinned and the other annotated.
;;==== DPDC-G19 - XIv_MappedCreditOrDebitDPDC: nonces and amounts must be the same length · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [DPDC-G19 - XIv_MappedCreditOrDebitDPDC: nonces and amounts must be the same length · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (ref-DPDC-C:module{DpdcCreateV2} DPDC-C)
        (sf:string "MOCKS-98c486052a51")
    )
    (map print
        [
            (expect-failure "<<DPDC-G19>> two nonces against one amount is refused"
                "Invalid <nonces> and <amounts> lengths for CreditOrDebit Operation"
                (ref-DPDC-C::XIv_MappedCreditOrDebitDPDC "ghost-acct" sf true [1 2] [1] true))
            ;;...and the other way round, because the check is `=` on both lists and not just a
            ;;"enough amounts to cover the nonces" bound.
            (expect-failure "<<DPDC-G19>> ...and one nonce against two amounts likewise"
                "Invalid <nonces> and <amounts> lengths for CreditOrDebit Operation"
                (ref-DPDC-C::XIv_MappedCreditOrDebitDPDC "ghost-acct" sf true [1] [1 2] true))
            ;;THE EDGE THAT MATTERS: two EMPTY lists are equal, so they clear this enforce. The map
            ;;below then runs over (enumerate 0 -1) -- which in Pact is the DESCENDING pair [0 -1],
            ;;NOT the empty list. So the empty call does not no-op; it indexes into empty lists and
            ;;dies on a native fault. Pinned so that a future "harmless empty input" assumption has
            ;;something to trip over.
            (expect-failure "<<DPDC-G19>> ...while two EMPTY lists pass the arity check and fault below it"
                "index out of bounds"
                (ref-DPDC-C::XIv_MappedCreditOrDebitDPDC "ghost-acct" sf true [] [] true))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "DPDC-I1 — INFO_DPSF|TransferNonce quote vs measured charge")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [DPDC-I1 · 01 · move one SFT nonce] ---")
;;FUNCTION COVERAGE (G6) — `INFO_DPSF|TransferNonce`, per the owner's spec: an INFO_ must report the same cost the
;;op actually charges. Template and rationale: `modules/ATS.repl <<ATS-I1>>`.
;;FIXTURE HAZARD, deliberate: this transfers MOCKS nonce 1, NOT nonce 3. The transfer family debits
;;the patron TWICE — once for gas, and again inside `DPDC-T::C_IgnisRoyaltyCollector`, which pays the
;;creator's ignis-royalty. The preview quotes only the gas leg. MOCKS nonce 3 carries a royalty of
;;9.0 and an ignis-royalty of 8.0 (written at DPDC-06), so measuring a transfer of nonce 3 would show
;;a charge larger than the quote and look like a preview defect when it is a second, separate charge.
;;Nonces 1, 2 and 4 all carry 0.0, so the measurement isolates the leg the preview is responsible for.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-TS02-C1:module{TalosStageTwo_ClientOneV2} TS02-C1)
        (ref-DPDC:module{DpdcV2} DPDC)
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
        (sf:string "MOCKS-98c486052a51")
        (nf:string "MOCKN-98c486052a51")
        (patron:string KST.ANHD)
        (lumy:string KST.LUMY)
        (emma:string KST.EMMA)
    )
    (let
        (
            (predicted:object{OuronetInfoV2.ClientInfo} (INFO-TWO.INFO_DPSF|TransferNonce patron sf patron lumy 1 2 false))
            (ignis-before:decimal (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply patron false))
            (m (ref-TS02-C1::DPSF|C_TransferNonce patron patron lumy sf 1 2 false))
        )
        (map print
            [
                (expect "<<DPDC-I1>> the preview's quote equals what the op actually charged"
                    (- ignis-before (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply patron false))
                    (at "ignis-need" (at "ignis" predicted)))
                (expect "<<DPDC-I1>> ...and it is a real, non-zero charge"
                    true (> (- ignis-before (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply patron false)) 0.0))
            ]
        )
    )
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(rollback-tx)

